"""Fused matmul + bias (broadcastable) Triton implementation.

out = input @ other + bias, with bias broadcastable to (M, N):
  scalar () / (1,) / (1, N) / (M, 1) / (M, N).

All numerics are produced by the Triton kernel; the host wrapper only reads
metadata (shapes/strides/dtype), validates shapes, allocates the fresh output
and launches.

Tile selection: a bounded Triton autotune search runs once per
(shape, element-size) key; the winning configuration is cached and every later
call for that key launches the raw JIT kernel directly, so tuned kernels do not
pay the tuner's per-call Python overhead.  Degenerate shapes (M, N or K below a
warp tile) bypass the tuner and use a small fixed configuration.
"""

